    {
      "rule": {
        "id": "particule-theme-eun-neun",
        "title": {
          "fr": "La particule de thème 은/는",
          "en": "The topic particle 은/는"
        },
        "description": {
          "fr": "Marquer le thème de la phrase avec 은 après consonne finale et 는 après voyelle.",
          "en": "Mark the topic of the sentence with 은 after a final consonant and 는 after a vowel."
        },
        "explanation": {
          "fr": "En coréen, la particule 은/는 s'attache au mot dont on parle : le thème de la phrase. Elle correspond souvent à « quant à… » ou au sujet général en français. Le choix entre les deux formes est purement phonétique : si le mot se termine par une consonne finale (batchim), on ajoute 은 ; s'il se termine par une voyelle, on ajoute 는. Par exemple : 학생 + 은 → 학생은, mais 친구 + 는 → 친구는. Cette particule sert aussi à marquer un contraste entre deux éléments.",
          "en": "In Korean, the particle 은/는 attaches to the word the sentence is about: its topic. It often corresponds to \"as for…\" or to the general subject in English. The choice between the two forms is purely phonetic: if the word ends in a final consonant (batchim), add 은; if it ends in a vowel, add 는. For example: 학생 + 은 → 학생은, but 친구 + 는 → 친구는. This particle is also used to mark a contrast between two elements."
        },
        "prerequisite_lists": [
          "starter-greetings"
        ],
        "min_known_words": {
          "nom": 5
        },
        "applies_to_categories": [
          "nom",
          "lieu"
        ],
        "mechanics": {
          "type": "particle",
          "particle_forms": {
            "after_consonant": "은",
            "after_vowel": "는"
          }
        },
        "worked_examples": [
          {
            "target": "저는 학생이에요.",
            "translations": {
              "fr": "Moi, je suis étudiant.",
              "en": "I am a student."
            }
          },
          {
            "target": "선생님은 지금 학교에 있어요.",
